# This file is generated by dune, edit dune-project instead
opam-version: "2.0"
synopsis: "OCaml as a Tactic Language for Rocq"
description: """
Camltac is an OCaml plugin for Rocq that lets you run OCaml code within Rocq scripts. Camltac makes it possible to define OCaml meta-programs and tactics, and run them in the current Rocq state without the friction and boilerplate of setting up a plugin.

Camltac is both a tactic and a meta-programming language:

- As a tactic language, Camltac provides constructs inspired by Ltac2, including term quotations (`{%constr| … |}`), pattern matching (`match%rocq`), and antiquotations using ppx_rocq. Camltac makes it easy to define new tactics by providing the usual tacticals from Ltac2, and a dedicated FFI with Ltac and Ltac2.

- As a meta-programming language, Camltac offers a complete meta-programming experience by allowing access to Rocq's internal APIs and state. To ensure stability, Camltac includes the Ltac2 APIs which provide a simple entry point to meta-programming in OCaml."""
maintainer: ["Dario Halilovic"]
authors: ["Dario Halilovic"]
license: "LGPL-2.1-only"
tags: [
  "category:Miscellaneous/Rocq Extensions"
  "keyword:tactic"
  "keyword:ocaml"
  "keyword:ltac2"
  "logpath:Camltac"
  "date:2026-10-26"
]
homepage: "https://github.com/epfl-systemf/camltac"
bug-reports: "https://github.com/epfl-systemf/camltac/issues"
depends: [
  "ocaml" {>= "4.14"}
  "dune" {>= "3.17" & < "3.24"}
  "coq-core" {>= "9.0"}
  "rocq-core"
  "ppx_rocq"
  "rocq-mltac2"
  "ppx_deriving"
  "ocamlfind"
  "odoc" {with-doc}
]
build: [
  [
    "dune"
    "build"
    "-p"
    name
    "-j"
    jobs
    "@install"
    "@runtest" {with-test}
    "@doc" {with-doc}
  ]
]
dev-repo: "git+https://github.com/epfl-systemf/camltac.git"
